{"record_type":"knowledge-corpus-map/1","status":"proposed-reference-view","scope":"Selected meanings and bounded claims of nine identified manuscripts, six foundation units and 25 roadmap definitions; not exhaustive semantic extraction.","not_authority_for":["scientific truth","runtime permission","publication acceptance","index admission","Muneral state or readiness"],"snapshot_policy":"Each document uses its own immutable source pin. Proposal pins are not a coherent accepted release. Rebase or merge requires a fresh graph snapshot and review of changed endpoints.","sources":{"corpus":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"ea0c30575d56e793fb2875df47126ab3f6dc30ad"},"f01":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"61d674244f70002e20506b387b210fd584074ad2"},"roadmap":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"42a10bd178e003f9615e8a58f8bfb7cf9d76c07b"},"transformations":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"2b863b45441da4b6dc6bdcadec046290285aed50"},"retrieval":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"ef6e223a9be6ac1a420556c07e584f0369bdc41f"},"interaction":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"8273f4eaf8bcf97de9a34c7890f0e54da3eecf45"},"evidence":{"repository":"Arcanada-one/knowledge-contract","commit":"b97ecd3f650f4aab566860c4a21b754ffd15a18a"}},"documents":[{"id":"D01","kind":"document","slug":"controlled-knowledge-reuse","title":"Knowledge Contracts and the Admission of Prepared Knowledge","source":"corpus","path":"papers/controlled-knowledge-reuse/PAPER.md","status":"accepted-source"},{"id":"D02","kind":"document","slug":"semantic-objects-and-context","title":"Semantic Objects, Context, and Conditions of Applicability","source":"corpus","path":"papers/semantic-objects-and-context/PAPER.md","status":"accepted-source"},{"id":"D03","kind":"document","slug":"constrained-transformations","title":"Constrained Transformations and the Limits of Knowledge Transfer","source":"transformations","path":"papers/constrained-transformations/PAPER.md","status":"editorial-proposal"},{"id":"D04","kind":"document","slug":"retrieval-and-context-composition","title":"Retrieval, Coverage, and Context Composition under Resource Limits","source":"retrieval","path":"papers/retrieval-and-context-composition/PAPER.md","status":"editorial-proposal"},{"id":"D05","kind":"document","slug":"interaction-and-memory","title":"Interaction, Documents, and Memory with Explicit Revision Boundaries","source":"interaction","path":"papers/interaction-and-memory/PAPER.md","status":"editorial-proposal"},{"id":"D06","kind":"document","slug":"evidence-and-falsification","title":"Evidence, Reasoning, and Falsification in Knowledge Systems","source":"evidence","path":"papers/evidence-and-falsification/PAPER.md","status":"editorial-proposal"},{"id":"D07","kind":"document","slug":"revision-and-governance","title":"Knowledge Revision, Version Identity, and the Adoption of Norms","source":"corpus","path":"papers/revision-and-governance/PAPER.md","status":"accepted-source"},{"id":"D08","kind":"document","slug":"knowledge-utility","title":"Knowledge Utility, Resource Accounting, and Lifecycle Decisions","source":"corpus","path":"papers/knowledge-utility/PAPER.md","status":"accepted-source"},{"id":"D09","kind":"document","slug":"human-meaning-and-computable-knowledge","title":"From Human Meaning to Contract-Governed Knowledge","source":"f01","path":"papers/human-meaning-and-computable-knowledge/PAPER.md","status":"research-draft"}],"terms":[{"id":"T01","kind":"term","label":"Knowledge Contract","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"A versioned specification of knowledge, intended use, grounds, dependencies, constraints and assessment obligations; not truth or execution authority."},{"id":"T02","kind":"term","label":"Semantic object","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"An addressable, versioned interpretation with content, attribution, context and grounds; not necessarily a retrieval chunk."},{"id":"T03","kind":"term","label":"Interpretation","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"A reading under stated assumptions; several readings can remain possible."},{"id":"T04","kind":"term","label":"Context","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"Conditions needed to interpret or use content, including relevant referents, scope, time, exceptions and recipient."},{"id":"T05","kind":"term","label":"Constraint","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"A condition restricting admissible interpretation, transformation, delivery or action; distinct from an acceptance criterion."},{"id":"T06","kind":"term","label":"Protected property","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Knowledge and its representation","reading_summary":"An observation or relation that a transformation is required to preserve."},{"id":"T07","kind":"term","label":"Coverage","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Retrieval, composition and reuse","reading_summary":"Established support for required slots of a named request at a named stage; not keyword presence."},{"id":"T08","kind":"term","label":"Dependency closure","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Retrieval, composition and reuse","reading_summary":"The least set containing selected roots and their active mandatory dependencies in a declared graph; it does not discover omitted edges."},{"id":"T09","kind":"term","label":"Assessment","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Evidence, versions and review","reading_summary":"A method-bound judgment about a particular subject revision and property."},{"id":"T10","kind":"term","label":"Authority","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Requirements, work and agency","reading_summary":"The legitimate scope of decisions or actions supplied by an identified authorization basis."},{"id":"T11","kind":"term","label":"Revision","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Evidence, versions and review","reading_summary":"An immutable identified content state; distinct from the mutable current selection."},{"id":"T12","kind":"term","label":"Evidence","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Evidence, versions and review","reading_summary":"An addressed observation or record supporting a specified claim under a method and trust boundary."},{"id":"T13","kind":"term","label":"Work Item","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Requirements, work and agency","reading_summary":"One goal-bearing unit with versioned requirements, constraints, assignments, attempts and acceptance criteria."},{"id":"T14","kind":"term","label":"Skill","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Requirements, work and agency","reading_summary":"A reusable description of a method and its conditions; the file is not evidence that its reader can perform it."},{"id":"T15","kind":"term","label":"Admission","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Retrieval, composition and reuse","reading_summary":"A decision permitting a particular use under specified requirements, policy and trust boundary."},{"id":"T16","kind":"term","label":"Knowledge utility","source":"corpus","path":"reference/glossary/GLOSSARY.md","section":"Retrieval, composition and reuse","reading_summary":"Task-, policy- and horizon-dependent benefit relative to a stated baseline and cost model; not an intrinsic document score."}],"claims":[{"id":"C01","kind":"claim","document":"D01","source_location":"4. Conditional preservation theorem","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"The paper supplies sufficient conditions under which prepared knowledge is admitted for a new use; prior completion alone does not supply that justification.","premises":["Sound prior verification","Complete unchanged relevant state and request observations","Preservation for every permitted output","Coverage of new artifact requirements","Discharge of current-use obligations"],"limits":"Not a necessary characterization of every possible justification; not automatic dependency discovery, existence of an output or runtime enforcement.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C02","kind":"claim","document":"D02","source_location":"3. Context and applicability","claim_kind":"conceptual-distinction","plain_meaning":"Applicability belongs to a specified use and its conditions, not to a context-free label of validity.","premises":["Identified interpretation and request scope","Mandatory conditions discharged, including a justified exemption when applicable"],"limits":"Unknown mandatory conditions do not become pass; a source statement is not automatically an endorsement or grant.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C03","kind":"claim","document":"D03","source_location":"3. Composition and preservation","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"For successful finite chains, compatible step conditions and agreed intermediate observations provide sufficient grounds for endpoint preservation.","premises":["Successful finite chain","Each local contract preserves its declared observation","Postcondition implies the next precondition","Adjacent observation functions agree on the relevant intermediate states"],"limits":"No termination or output-existence guarantee; failure of a premise blocks this proof, not necessarily every individual successful path.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C04","kind":"claim","document":"D04","source_location":"Scope across the complete manuscript","claim_kind":"modeling-obligation","plain_meaning":"Selecting a dependency-complete set does not establish that the necessary conditions survived in the delivered context.","premises":["Declared request coverage","Complete relevant dependencies in the selected model","Admissible resource and current-use conditions","Preservation or re-establishment in the actual delivered representation"],"limits":"A closed graph is not a semantic delivery test; the finite selection models are not production KC conformance.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C05","kind":"claim","document":"D05","source_location":"5. Conditional transition properties","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"An earlier requirement generation cannot become current solely because its old completion event arrives late.","premises":["Work Item and non-reissued generation identities","Comparison at the same serialization point as making the result current","Otherwise a new assessment bound to the actual output and active generation"],"limits":"Not interpretation correctness or selection among same-generation attempts; internal atomic replay handling is not external exactly-once execution.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C06","kind":"claim","document":"D06","source_location":"3. Justification graphs and conditional soundness","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"A finite acyclic derivation preserves truth when its premises, rules and side conditions satisfy the stated semantics.","premises":["One fixed domain model","True premises","Sound applied rules","Satisfied side conditions","Finite acyclic derivation"],"limits":"A graph-shaped explanation does not establish these premises, semantic extraction or implementation compliance.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C07","kind":"claim","document":"D07","source_location":"Proposition 3. Complete dependencies identify candidates for reassessment","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"Reverse reachability finds all potentially affected assessments only relative to a complete represented dependency graph.","premises":["Every relevant dependency represented","Finite graph","Complete reverse traversal"],"limits":"Affected does not mean false; alternative sufficient grounds can remain, and an omitted edge defeats completeness.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C08","kind":"claim","document":"D08","source_location":"Proposition 2. A simple reuse policy has a conditional break-even point","claim_kind":"conditional-deduction","plain_meaning":"In the restricted accounting model, reuse costs less exactly when its preparation and all admitted-hit costs are below the valid cold-route cost.","premises":["Same acceptance conditions","Nonnegative costs in one unit and horizon","At least one request","No intervening invalidation or additional omitted cost"],"limits":"Not measured savings, causal benefit, universally fair allocation or permission to skip checks.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"},{"id":"C09","kind":"claim","document":"D09","source_location":"4. A bounded semantic bridge","claim_kind":"conceptual-interface","plain_meaning":"A representation is assessed against declared task-relevant distinctions rather than identified with all human meaning.","premises":["Fixed interpretation and observation profile","Explicit source/context/attribution","Nonempty and justified operational assessment domain"],"limits":"Set-theoretic factorization is not an effective decoder, universal human semantics or evidence of extraction accuracy.","assessment":"producer-summary-not-independent-review"}],"foundation_units":[{"id":"F01","kind":"manuscript-unit","title":"From Human Meaning to Contract-Governed Knowledge","d